sentence'" seems long-winded. Is there not a generic way to refer to "this =
(entire) text"? I mean "text" as it is used in literary theory, not just on=
ly actual text, so it could be a speech, etc..

Could I say this?

mi ze'u ciska ti


Was there something wrong with the logical implication of ni'i? "Plipe is a=
 grasshopper, thus Plipe eats grass" is what I meant.


